  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @addtogroup variance
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @{
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  */
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c **** 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @brief Variance of the elements of a Q31 vector.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrc points to the input vector
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @param[in]       blockSize length of the input vector
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @param[out]      *pResult variance value returned here
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * @details
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  *\par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * The input is represented in 1.31 format, which is then downshifted by 8 bits
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * which yields 1.23, and intermediate multiplication yields a 2.46 format.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * The accumulator maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplication results,
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * but provides only a 16 guard bits.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * There is no saturation on intermediate additions.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * If the accumulator overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * log2(blockSize)-8 bits, as a total of blockSize additions are performed internally.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * After division, internal variables should be Q18.46
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  * Finally, the 18.46 accumulator is right shifted by 15 bits to yield a 1.31 format value.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c ****  */
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/StatisticsFunctions/arm_var_q31.c **** 
